test.yaml:7:40: writing to "GITHUB_OUTPUT" creates a file with that name in the working directory, because without a `$` it is not the variable: the runner never sees it, so nothing is set as an output of the step. write `"$GITHUB_OUTPUT"` [environment-file-redirect]
test.yaml:8:31: writing to "GITHUB_ENV" creates a file with that name in the working directory, because without a `$` it is not the variable: the runner never sees it, so nothing is set as an environment variable of the next steps. write `"$GITHUB_ENV"` [environment-file-redirect]
test.yaml:9:33: writing to "GITHUB_PATH" creates a file with that name in the working directory, because without a `$` it is not the variable: the runner never sees it, so nothing is added to the PATH of the next steps. write `"$GITHUB_PATH"` [environment-file-redirect]
test.yaml:10:40: writing to "GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY" creates a file with that name in the working directory, because without a `$` it is not the variable: the runner never sees it, so nothing is shown in the summary of the job. write `"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"` [environment-file-redirect]
test.yaml:11:32: writing to "GITHUB_STATE" creates a file with that name in the working directory, because without a `$` it is not the variable: the runner never sees it, so nothing is saved as the state of the step. write `"$GITHUB_STATE"` [environment-file-redirect]
test.yaml:16:16: writing to "GITHUB_OUTPUT" creates a file with that name in the working directory, because without a `$` it is not the variable: the runner never sees it, so nothing is set as an output of the step. write `"$GITHUB_OUTPUT"` [environment-file-redirect]
test.yaml:19:27: writing to "GITHUB_OUTPUT" creates a file with that name in the working directory, because without a `$` it is not the variable: the runner never sees it, so nothing is set as an output of the step. write `"$GITHUB_OUTPUT"` [environment-file-redirect]
test.yaml:26:22: `>` empties $GITHUB_OUTPUT before it writes, so what this script wrote to it before is lost. append with `>>` [environment-file-redirect]
test.yaml:29:28: `tee` without `-a` empties $GITHUB_ENV before it writes, so what this script wrote to it before is lost. append with `tee -a` [environment-file-redirect]
test.yaml:33:24: `>` empties $GITHUB_OUTPUT before it writes, so what this script wrote to it before is lost. append with `>>` [environment-file-redirect]
